{
  "documents": {
    "0": {
      "doc_id": 0,
      "title": "dummy_01",
      "content": "DocuVault is a Python document search system that ingests text files from a folder.\nEach document receives an identifier, a title, its content, and an absolute source path.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_01.txt"
    },
    "1": {
      "doc_id": 1,
      "title": "dummy_02",
      "content": "Document ingestion reads every .txt file and stores its content in the knowledge base.\nThe file name becomes the document title, while UTF-8 decoding preserves text reliably.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_02.txt"
    },
    "2": {
      "doc_id": 2,
      "title": "dummy_03",
      "content": "Text cleaning converts document content to lowercase before vectorization.\nPunctuation is removed so terms such as Search, search, and search. match consistently.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_03.txt"
    },
    "3": {
      "doc_id": 3,
      "title": "dummy_04",
      "content": "The vocabulary contains every unique cleaned word found across the document collection.\nSorting the vocabulary gives each word a stable position in every document vector.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_04.txt"
    },
    "4": {
      "doc_id": 4,
      "title": "dummy_05",
      "content": "Word frequencies count how often each cleaned term appears in a document.\nA frequency dictionary is converted into a vector using the shared knowledge base vocabulary.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_05.txt"
    },
    "5": {
      "doc_id": 5,
      "title": "dummy_06",
      "content": "Cosine similarity compares document vectors by measuring the angle between them.\nDocuments with more shared terms receive a higher similarity score during search.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_06.txt"
    },
    "6": {
      "doc_id": 6,
      "title": "dummy_07",
      "content": "A query can be cleaned and vectorized with the same vocabulary as stored documents.\nUsing the same preprocessing pipeline keeps query and document vectors comparable.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_07.txt"
    },
    "7": {
      "doc_id": 7,
      "title": "dummy_08",
      "content": "The knowledge base stores vectors in a dictionary keyed by each document identifier.\nKeeping the document and vector maps aligned makes search results easy to trace to source files.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_08.txt"
    },
    "8": {
      "doc_id": 8,
      "title": "dummy_09",
      "content": "A document preview can use the title and the first part of its content for display.\nThe source path allows an application to open the original text after a search result is selected.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_09.txt"
    },
    "9": {
      "doc_id": 9,
      "title": "dummy_10",
      "content": "Search quality depends on useful vocabulary, consistent cleaning, and meaningful document content.\nAdding related terms across documents creates realistic overlap for cosine similarity experiments.\n",
      "source_path": "D:\\Mine\\Learning_Related\\AI-Engineer-Practice\\ai-engineer\\projects\\docuvault\\docs\\dummy_10.txt"
    },
    "10": {
